# Safe-area inset watch (ALGR)

Every Labs **webapp that may become a native store build** (Capacitor / CapGo / WKWebView) must keep chrome clear of the notch, status bar, home indicator, and display cutouts.

## Hard rules

1. **`viewport-fit=cover`** on the app `index.html` viewport meta so `env(safe-area-inset-*)` is non-zero under native shells.
2. **Prefer `env(safe-area-inset-*)`** (with `0px` fallback) for fixed headers, bottom nav, FABs, sheets, full-bleed auth/marketing screens — do **not** hard-code notch/home-indicator padding.
3. **Install a safe-area inset watch** at app boot that mirrors insets onto CSS variables and **re-applies on orientation / visualViewport / resize** (native WebViews can change insets after first paint).
4. When Cap / native StatusBar is used, **overlay the WebView** and rely on safe-area padding (see Miles2Go `initNativeStatusBar`) — do not draw interactive controls under the status bar.
5. Marketing-only / static sites without SPA chrome may skip the JS watch, but still use `viewport-fit=cover` + env insets on any fixed UI.

Full playbook: `docs/prompts/safe-area-inset-watch.md`. Template: ALGR `scraps/safe-area-inset-watch/templates/installSafeAreaInsetWatch.js`.
